1.  Some formatting seems to have been lost in the HTML version.  It would be 
worth setting up something in the stylesheet to render Lojban words 
differently to English (I just used the EM tag in the original, but a 
different font might be appropriate).  I noticed that there is a reference to 
lojbanlevel0.css but I couldn't find the file.  Quotation marks seem to be 
missing.

2.  I can't turn the TeX version into DVI - I get an "undefined control 
sequence" error message. Since Nick says that he doesn't use TeX, maybe some 
TeXperts on this list could check this out.

3.  Someone mailed me a while back, pointing out that "mi'e" is pronounced 
less like English "me hey" (as I wrote) and more liek "me heh".  Might be 
worth changing this to avoid an excessively long "e".

